Z||000000||Cozmo||05-25-2001||08:09 AM||||The "soon-to-be in the GT engine" ('88 vin C 3800, still in the donor car) is blowing a code 65 (EGR). It runs rough at cruising speeds and the TC jumps in and out.  It is a "digital" EGR with 3 solenoids (what a weird <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> design!).  This sucker is EXPENSIVE ($145) and I was wondering if this thing can be "serviced" (taken apart and cleaned).  I have to go to the boneyard this weekend, if I find one I'll grab it.<BR>Anyone have any experience and hints about this odd EGR? <BR>Thanks<P>------------------<BR><B>C02M0</B><BR><I>Suncoast Fieros</I><BR>'85 silver 2M6 4spd. Targa <B>"Silver Streak"</B><BR>'86 black auto GT <B>"Blackbird"</B><BR>'87 white auto Coupe <B>"The Duke"</B>||||reg||5
Z||000001||elfiero||05-25-2001||11:51 AM||||this code means the ECM doesnt like voltage<BR>going thru the EGR. this means replace the<BR>EGR.The only service you can do to it is<BR>clean out the carbon build-up-I don't think<BR>this can cause a code,but I guess it would'nt<BR>hurt to check it!||||reg||6
Z||000002||terryk||05-25-2001||12:58 PM||||Yep, and there is a problem with the solenoid surfaces clogging and the thing leaks. Any other digital will work. No, you can't service any part of it.<P>Interesting concept but they don't wear well.||||reg||1
